{
  "title": "Dua for Fending Off Distress, Grief, and Fear",
  "data": "Ya Absar al-Nazirin ×70\nWhen something frightening befalls you, face the qiblah and pray two units. Then recite 70 times, presenting your request each time you reach the end:\nيَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِيْنَ\nYAA ABSARAN NAAZIREEN\nO Most Seeing of seers,\nيَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِيْنَ\nYAA ASMA'AS SAAMI'EEN\nO Most Hearing of hearers,\nيَا اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ\nYAA ASRA'AL HAASIBEEN\nO Swiftest of reckoners,\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of the merciful.",
  "tabs": [
    "Allahu Rabbi La Ushriku Bihi\nIn distress, grief, anxiety or hardship, recite:\nاَللهُ رَبِّىْ لَا اُشْرِكُ بِهٖ شَيْئًا\nALLAAHU RABBEE LAA USHRIKU BIHEE SHAY'AA\nAllah is my Lord; I associate nothing with Him.\nتَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ\nTAWAKKALTU A'LAL HAYYIL LADHEE LAA YAMOOT\nI put my trust in the Ever-Living Who never dies.",
    "Dua of Prophet Yusuf in the Well\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّى اَسْئَلُكَ بِاَنَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BI-ANNA LAKAL HAMD\nO Allah, I ask You, for to You belongs all praise;\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ الْمَنَّانُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTAL MANNAAN\nthere is no god but You, the Bestower of favors,\nبَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ذُو الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nBADEE'US SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI DHUL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nthe Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of Majesty and Honor,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nthat You bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَّاَنْ تَجْعَلَ لِىْ مِمَّا اَنَا فِيْهِ فَرَجًا وَمَخْرَجًا\nWA AN TAJ'ALA LEE MIMMAA ANAA FEEHI FARAJAN WA MAKHRAJAA\nand that You grant me relief and a way out of the plight I am in.",
    "When You Fear Something\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ لَا يَكْفٰى مِنْكَ اَحَدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA LAA YAKFAA MINKA AHAD\nO Allah, no one can suffice against You,\nوَاَنْتَ تَكْفٰى مِنْ كُلِّ اَحَدٍ مِّنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA ANTA TAKFAA MIN KULLI AHADIM MIN KHALQIK\nwhile You suffice against everyone of Your creation;\nفَاَكْفِنِىْ كَذَا وَكَذَا\nFA-AKFINEE KADHAA WA KADHAA\nso suffice me against such-and-such.\nIn place of \"such-and-such\", name what you fear.\nAnother narrated form:\nیَا كَافِيًا مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَلَا يَكْفٰى مِنْكَ شَىْءٌ فِى السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nYAA KAAFIYAN MIN KULLI SHAY'IN WA LAA YAKFAA MINKA SHAY'UN FIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nO You Who suffices against everything, while nothing in the heavens and the earth can suffice against You,\nاِكْفِنِىْ مَا اَهَمَّنِىْ مِنْ اَمْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nIKFINEE MAA AHAMMANEE MIN AMRID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nsuffice me in what concerns me of the affairs of this world and the Hereafter,\nوَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ\nWA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nand bless Muhammad and his family.",
    "Before Facing a Feared Ruler\nBefore going to a ruler you fear, recite:\nبِاللّٰهِ اَسْتَفْتِحُ وَبِاللّٰهِ اَسْتَنْجِحُ\nBILLAAHI ASTAFTIHU WA BILLAAHI ASTANJIH\nBy Allah I seek an opening, and by Allah I seek success,\nوَبِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ اَتَوَجَّهُ\nWA BIMUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE ATAWAJJAH\nand through Muhammad, Allah bless him and his family, I turn [to You].\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ذَلِّلْ لِىْ صُعُوْبَتَهٗ وَسَهِّلْ لِىْ حُزُوْنَتَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA DHALLIL LEE SU'OOBATAHOO WA SAHHIL LEE HUZOONATAH\nO Allah, subdue for me his harshness and ease for me his roughness,\nفَاِنَّكَ تَمْحُوْ مَا تَشَاۤءُ وَتُثْبِتُ وَعِنْدَكَ اُمُّ الْكِتَابِ\nFA-INNAKA TAMHOO MAA TASHAA'U WA TUTHBITU WA I'NDAKA UMMUL KITAAB\nfor You erase what You will and confirm [what You will], and with You is the Mother of the Book.\nحَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nHASBIYALLAAHU LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA A'LAYHI TAWAKKALTU WA HUWA RABBUL A'RSHIL A'ZEEM\nAllah suffices me; there is no god but He; in Him I trust, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne.\nوَاَمْتَنِعُ بِحَوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَقُوَّتِهٖ مِنْ حَوْلِهِمْ وَقُوَّتِهِمْ\nWA AMTANI'U BIHAWLILLAAHI WA QUWWATIHEE MIN HAWLIHIM WA QUWWATIHIM\nI take refuge in the might and power of Allah from their might and power,\nوَاَمْتَنِعُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ\nWA AMTANI'U BIRABBIL FALAQI MIN SHARRI MAA KHALAQ\nand I take refuge in the Lord of the Daybreak from the evil of what He has created.\nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAH\nThere is no might and no power save in Allah.",
    "Dua of Imam al-Baqir in Distress\nWhen something distressing happens, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَّاغْفِرْ لِىْ وَارْحَمْنِىْ وَزَكِّ عَمَلِىْ\nWAGHFIR LEE WARHAMNEE WA ZAKKI A'MALEE\nforgive me, have mercy on me, purify my deeds,\nوَيَسِّرْ مُنْقَلَبِىْ وَاهْدِ قَلْبِىْ وَاٰمِنْ خَوْفِىْ\nWA YASSIR MUNQALABEE WAHDI QALBEE WA AAMIN KHAWFEE\nease my return, guide my heart, and calm my fear,\nوَعَافِنِىْ فِىْ عُمْرِىْ كُلِّهٖ وَثَبِّتْ حُجَّتِىْ\nWA A'AFINEE FEE U'MREE KULLIHEE WA THABBIT HUJJATEE\ngrant me well-being throughout my whole life, and make firm my proof,\nوَاغْفِرْ خَطَايَاىَ وَبَيِّضْ وَجْهِىْ\nWAGHFIR KHATAAYAAYA WA BAYYID WAJHEE\nforgive my sins, and whiten my face,\nوَاعْصِمْنِىْ فِىْ دِيْنِىْ وَسَهِّلْ مَطْلَبِىْ\nWA'SIMNEE FEE DEENEE WA SAHHIL MATLABEE\nprotect me in my religion, ease my quest,\nوَوَسِّعْ عَلَىَّ فِىْ رِزْقِىْ فَاِنِّىْ ضَعِيْفٌ\nWA WASSI' A'LAYYA FEE RIZQEE FA-INNEE DA'EEF\nand widen my sustenance, for I am weak.\nوَتَجَاوَزْ عَنْ سَيِّئِ مَا عِنْدِىْ بِحُسْنِ مَا عِنْدَكَ\nWA TAJAAWAZ A'N SAYYI'I MAA I'NDEE BIHUSNI MAA I'NDAK\nOverlook the evil that is with me through the good that is with You.\nوَلَا تَفْجَعْنِىْ بِنَفْسِىْ وَلَا تَفْجَعْ لِىْ حَمِيْمًا\nWA LAA TAFJA'NEE BINAFSEE WA LAA TAFJA' LEE HAMEEMAA\nDo not bring me grief through my own self, nor grieve me through a loved one.\nوَهَبْ لِىْ يَا اِلٰهِىْ لَحْظَةً مِنْ لَحَظَاتِكَ\nWA HAB LEE YAA ILAAHEE LAHZATAN MIN LAHAZAATIK\nGrant me, O my God, one glance of Your glances\nتَكْشِفُ بِهَا عَنِّىْ جَمِيْعَ مَا بِهِ ابْتَلَيْتَنِىْ\nTAKSHIFU BIHAA A'NNEE JAMEE'A MAA BIHIB TALAYTANEE\nby which You lift from me all that You have tried me with,\nوَتَرُدُّ بِهَا عَلَىَّ مَا هُوَ اَحْسَنُ عَادَتِكَ عِنْدِىْ\nWA TARUDDU BIHAA A'LAYYA MAA HUWA AHSANU A'ADATIKA I'NDEE\nand by which You return to me the best of Your custom with me.\nفَقَدْ ضَعُفَتْ قُوَّتِىْ وَقَلَّتْ حِيْلَتِىْ\nFAQAD DA'UFAT QUWWATEE WA QALLAT HEELATEE\nMy strength has weakened and my means have dwindled;\nوَانْقَطَعَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ رَجَاۤئِىْ وَلَمْ يَبْقَ اِلَّا رَجَاۤؤُكَ وَتَوَكُّلِىْ عَلَيْكَ\nWANQATA'A MIN KHALQIKA RAJAA'EE WA LAM YABQA ILLAA RAJAA'UKA WA TAWAKKULEE A'LAYK\nmy hope in Your creation is cut off, and nothing remains but hope in You and my trust in You.\nوَقُدْرَتُكَ عَلَىَّ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تَرْحَمَنِىْ وَتُعَافِيَنِىْ\nWA QUDRATUKA A'LAYYA YAA RABBI AN TARHAMANEE WA TU'AAFIYANEE\nYour power over me, O Lord, to have mercy on me and grant me well-being\nكَقُدْرَتِكَ عَلَىَّ اَنْ تُعَذِّبَنِىْ وَتَبْتَلِيَنِىْ\nKAQUDRATIKA A'LAYYA AN TU'ADHDHIBANEE WA TABTALIYANEE\nis like Your power over me to punish me and to try me.\nاِلٰهِىْ ذِكْرُ عَوَايِدِكَ يُؤْنِسُنِىْ\nILAAHEE DHIKRU A'WAAYIDIKA YU'NISUNEE\nMy God, remembering Your customary favors comforts me,\nوَالرَّجَاۤءُ لِاِنْعَامِكَ يُقَوِّيْنِىْ\nWAR RAJAA'U LI-IN'AAMIKA YUQAWWEENEE\nhope for Your blessings strengthens me,\nوَلَمْ اَخْلُ مِنْ نِعَمِكَ مُنْذُ خَلَقْتَنِىْ\nWA LAM AKHLU MIN NI'AMIKA MUNDHU KHALAQTANEE\nand I have not been without Your blessings since You created me.\nفَاَنْتَ رَبِّىْ وَسَيِّدِىْ وَمَفْزَعِىْ وَمَلْجَاىَ\nFA-ANTA RABBEE WA SAYYIDEE WA MAFZA'EE WA MALJAAY\nYou are my Lord, my Master, my refuge and my shelter,\nوَالْحَافِظُ لِىْ وَالذَّآبُّ عَنِّىْ وَالرَّحِيْمُ بِىْ وَالْمُتَكَفِّلُ بِرِزْقِىْ\nWAL HAAFIZU LEE WADH DHAABBU A'NNEE WAR RAHEEMU BEE WAL MUTAKAFFILU BIRIZQEE\nmy Guardian, my Defender, the One Merciful to me, and the Guarantor of my sustenance.\nوَفِىْ قَضَاۤئِكَ وَقُدْرَتِكَ كُلُّ مَا اَنَا فِيْهِ\nWA FEE QADAA'IKA WA QUDRATIKA KULLU MAA ANAA FEEH\nIn Your decree and Your power lies all that I am in;\nفَلْيَكُنْ يَّا سَيِّدِىْ وَمَوْلَاىَ فِيْمَا قَضَيْتَ وَقَدَّرْتَ وَحَتَمْتَ\nFALYAKUN YAA SAYYIDEE WA MAWLAAYA FEEMAA QADAYTA WA QADDARTA WA HATAMT\nso let there be, O my Master and my Lord, in what You have decreed, ordained and made certain,\nتَعْجِيْلُ خَلَاصِىْ مِمَّا اَنَا فِيْهِ جَمِيْعِهٖ وَالْعَافِيَةُ لِىْ\nTA'JEELU KHALAASEE MIMMAA ANAA FEEHI JAMEE'IHEE WAL A'AFIYATU LEE\na speedy deliverance for me from all that I am in, and well-being for me;\nفَاِنِّىْ لَا اَجِدُ لِدَفْعِ ذٰلِكَ اَحَدًا غَيْرَكَ وَلَا اَعْتَمِدُ فِيْهِ اِلَّا عَلَيْكَ\nFA-INNEE LAA AJIDU LIDAF'I DHAALIKA AHADAN GHAYRAKA WA LAA A'TAMIDU FEEHI ILLAA A'LAYK\nfor I find none but You to ward this off, nor do I rely on anyone in it but You.\nفَكُنْ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ عِنْدَ اَحْسَنِ ظَنِّىْ بِكَ وَرَجَاۤئِىْ لَكَ\nFAKUN YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAMI I'NDA AHSANI ZANNEE BIKA WA RAJAA'EE LAK\nSo be, O Lord of Majesty and Honor, as my best thought of You and my hope in You.\nوَارْحَمْ تَضَرُّعِىْ وَاسْتِكَانَتِىْ وَضَعْفَ رُكْنِىْ\nWARHAM TADARRU'EE WASTIKAANATEE WA DA'FA RUKNEE\nHave mercy on my pleading, my humility and the weakness of my support,\nوَامْنُنْ بِذٰلِكَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلٰى كُلِّ دَاعٍ دَعَاكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWAMNUN BIDHAALIKA A'LAYYA WA A'LAA KULLI DAA'IN DA'AAKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand grant this as a favor to me and to everyone who calls upon You, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nAnd Allah bless Muhammad and his family."
  ],
  "merits": "Ya Absar al-Nazirin: Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) is reported to have said: Whenever a horrifying matter inflicts you, turn your face towards the qiblah and offer a two-unit prayer. Upon accomplishment, say this supplication seventy times, and submit your requests each time you come to its end.\n\nAllahu Rabbi: The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said: Whoever is inflicted by a distress, a grief, angst, or a hardship, may say this statement.\n\nDua of Prophet Yusuf: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: When his brothers threw (Prophet) Joseph in the well, Archangel Gabriel came to him and said, “O boy, what are you doing here?” Joseph answered, “My brothers have thrown me in this well.” “Do you like to come out of it?” asked the archangel. “This is up to Allah the Almighty and All-majestic,” answered Joseph, “If He wishes, He will do.” “Allah the All-exalted says to you that if you pray Me with this supplication, I will take you out of this well,” taught Gabriel. “What is this supplication?” asked Joseph, and Gabriel taught him this one. After that, the caravan came and took Prophet Joseph out of the well, as the Holy Qur’an has related.\n\nWhen you fear something: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Whenever you fear something, you may say this supplication. According to another tradition, you may say the second form.\n\nBefore a ruler: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) has also said: Whoever comes to a ruler whom he fears may say this supplication before entering his presence.\n\nDua of Imam al-Baqir: This supplication is reported to have been said by Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) whenever a distressing matter would take place."
}
